<!DOCTYPE faqs SYSTEM 'dtd/faqs.dtd'>
<faqs title='Building and Running FAQs'>
 <faq title='Recompiling source files?'>
  <q>How do I recompile the source files?</q>
  <a>
   <p>
    To build &ParserName; you need the Java Development
    Kit (JDK) version 1.8 (or higher) installed on your machine.
    The build is performed by
    <jump href='https://maven.apache.org/'>Maven</jump>.
    The source package includes the Maven wrapper (<code>mvnw</code>
    and <code>mvnw.cmd</code>), which downloads a suitable Maven
    version automatically, so no separate Maven installation is
    required.
   </p>
   <p>
    Before invoking the build, set the <code>JAVA_HOME</code>
    environment variable to the installed location of your JDK. Then,
    from the directory where you extracted &ParserName;, run:
   </p>
   <source>./mvnw clean package</source>
   <p>
    On Windows, use <code>mvnw.cmd clean package</code> instead. This
    compiles the source files and creates the JAR files in the
    <code>target</code> directory. To compile and run the tests as
    well, run <code>./mvnw clean verify</code>.
   </p>
   <p>
    The documentation, the distributions and the alternative jars are
    enabled with Maven profiles. For the complete list, see the
    <code>README.md</code> file in the source package.
   </p>
  </a>
 </faq>
 <faq title='Regenerating API documentation?'>
  <q>How do I regenerate the API documentation?</q>
  <a>
   <p>
    To regenerate the API documentation, you need to set up
    your environment to build &ParserName;.  Instead of running
    <code>./mvnw clean package</code>, run:
   </p>
   <source>./mvnw clean package -Pjavadocs</source>
   <p>
    The generated documentation is written to
    <code>target/docs/javadocs</code>.
   </p>
  </a>
 </faq>
